{
  "how_to_read": "Personal sessions: what a person tells Heliox, and whether it changes how Heliox talks and what it does after a restart. Read like sessions.json, plus: an 'event' of 'restart' starts a new session server over the same folder (what is on disk stays, the conversation does not); 'sent' and 'not_sent' are about what the fast model is sent in that turn (checked for every kind with a model); 'planned_with' is about what the planner is given; 'stored' and 'not_stored' are about everything on disk after the turn; 'never_sent' and 'never_stored' hold for the whole session. 'via': 'turn' dispatches as the listener does (PilotServer._voice_turn), with the personal context the daemon gives the layer. 'expect_cloud' holds for a model in the cloud only: a model on this computer may be sent more. 'config_saved_in_scratch' (turn): true, the turn saved the configuration; false, it wrote nothing; either way every save went inside the scratch root, never the person's folders; 'config' (turn): each dotted setting (as 'live.enabled') has that value in the scratch config.toml after the turn; 'real_config_untouched' (session): the person's own config folders are listed before and after (by the pytest folder guard under pytest) and must not change. Whether Heliox kept or changed something is checked on what was said ('has'/'not'): a reply that claims a change that did not happen, or denies one that did, fails the session. An 'event' of 'approve_setting' (with 'section' and 'values') is the person approving that setting change in Heliox's window, through the daemon's own dialog. 'receipts' (session): signed task receipts are kept in the session's folder, as the daemon keeps them. 'second_voice_guard' (session): the second-voice rule is on (pilot.conversation.reach), at its default threshold. 'second_voice_threshold' (session): that threshold instead of the default.",
